    "case_summary": "A 30-year-old baker from South India presented with six weeks of low-grade fever, fatigue, and progressive polyarthritis affecting the large joints of arms and legs. No small joint involvement and no diurnal variation were noted. No history of high-risk sexual behavior. No relevant past medical history.\n\nTemperature: 38.9°CMultiple dull red tender nodules on the forehead, left cheek, and sternumSolitary 1 × 1 cm firm right cervical lymph nodeActive arthritis of the knee, hip, and elbow joints bilaterallyLiver palpable 4 cm below the right costal margin (liver span 16 cm)Other examinations were normal\n\nLaboratory Tests:- Normal full blood count- Erythrocyte sedimentation rate: 6 mm/h- C-reactive protein: 131 mg/L (reference range <6 mg/L)- Negative for antinuclear antibodies, IgM-rheumatoid factor, antineutrophil cytoplasmic antibodies, antistreptolysin O, and anti-DNase B antibodies- Normal serum calcium and angiotensin-converting enzyme levels- Four blood cultures were sterile- Negative urine examination for Gonococci spp.- Negative serum Venereal Disease Research Laboratory test for syphilisImaging Studies:- Normal transthoracic echocardiogram- Normal radiographs of the affected joints- Chest radiograph findings:  Image Title: Bilateral upper and mid-zone chest radiograph  Image Description: Bilateral upper-zone and mid-zone parenchymal infiltrates with nodular lesions, worse on the left sidePathological Studies:- Skin lesion biopsy: Granulomatous inflammation with suppuration- Cervical lymph node biopsy:  Image Title: Lymph node histopathology  Image Description: Large areas of necrosis rimmed by epithelioid cell granulomas with occasional Langhans' multinucleated giant cells- Ziehl-Neelsen staining: Positive for acid-fast bacilli",
